---
HydroNode from your terminal: sensors, values, devices and live data.

Usage: hn [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Start:
  login        Sign in (browser, device code or API token)
  logout       Sign out and forget the stored login
  whoami       Show who you are signed in as
  status       Devices, anomalies and messages at a glance

Data:
  sensors      List, show, create, rename and delete sensors
  values       Summaries of a data point over time
  watch        Live values in the terminal
  set          Set a writable data point (switch, setpoint)
  command      Send a command to a device
  export       Download readings as CSV, JSON or Parquet

Devices:
  devices      Firmware, health and updates over the air
  console      What devices sent and why something was rejected
  push         Send a signed value like a device
  simulate     Run a fake device that sends signed values

More:
  anomalies    Open anomalies on your sensors
  messages     Your inbox
  stations     Public weather stations
  automations  List and switch automations
  tokens       API tokens for scripts and integrations
  sessions     Where you are signed in
  api          Send a raw API request
  config       Show and change settings
  profile      Servers and accounts (for example a second account)
  completion   Shell completion script
  open         Open HydroNode in the browser

Options:
  -p, --profile <NAME>  Profile to use (server and login), see 'hn profile list'
      --json            Print JSON instead of tables (stable shape, for scripts)
  -h, --help            Print help
  -V, --version         Print version

Run 'hn help <command>' for details. Docs: https://hydronode.tech/docs/guide/cli
